  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "The average (mean) of \\(20\\) numbers is \\(30,\\) and the average of \\(30\\) other numbers is \\(20.\\) What is the average of all \\(50\\) numbers?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(23\\)",
    "B": "\\(24\\)",
    "C": "\\(25\\)",
    "D": "\\(26\\)",
    "E": "\\(27\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The two groups have different sizes, so first recover each group's sum. Since mean equals sum divided by the number of entries, the sums are\n\\[\n20\\cdot30=600\\quad\\text{and}\\quad30\\cdot20=600.\n\\]\nAll fifty numbers therefore have sum \\(600+600=1200\\). Their mean is\n\\[\n\\frac{1200}{50}=24.\n\\]\nThus the answer is \\(\\boxed{24}\\), choice B.",
